    {
        "content": "<p>I think the reason for this one is quite obvious: Function application for <code>Matrix</code> is defeq abuse and unfolding <code>of</code> even more so.</p>",
        "id": 583014153,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1775043375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"321459\">@Damiano Testa</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span>!</p>\n<p>I've updated the adapation notes in that file explaining the defeq abuse underlying the change.</p>\n<p>I would encourage anyone and everyone to help explain adaptation notes --- not necessarily now as part of this PR, but constantly throughout Mathlib. I think a PR explaining (or removing) a single adaptation note is great --- otherwise we will accumulate these forever.</p>",
        "id": 583015718,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1775043807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For this PR, we can't wait to resolve all of these: that's going to have to happen out in Mathlib.</p>",
